{title: 365 - O Zion, Haste}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #365 • TIDINGS • 10.10.11.11}
{lyricist: Mary A. Thomson}
{composer: James Walch}
{key: Ab}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 365}
{meta: tune TIDINGS}
{meta: meter 10.10.11.11}
{meta: category Christian Church - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Ab]O Zion, [Bbm]haste, [Cm]thy [Eb7/Bb]mission [Ab/C]high fulfilling,
[Db]To tell to [Ab]all the [Eb7]world that God is [Ab]light,
[Ab]That He who made all [Cm]nations [Fm/C]isnot [Cm]willing
[Bbm]One soul [Eb/Bb]should [Ab]perish, [Cm]lost [Ab]in shades [Bbm]of [Eb]night.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Eb7]Publish glad [Ab]tidings, [Eb7]tidings of [Ab]peace;
[Fm]tidings of [Bbm]Jesus, [Db]redemption [Ab/Eb]and [Eb7]release.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Ab]Proclaim to [Bbm]every [Ab]people, tongue, [Eb7]and nation
[Db]that God, in [Ab]whom they [Eb7]live and move, is [Ab]love;
[Ab]tell how he stooped to [Cm]save [Fm/C]his lost [Cm]creation,
[Bbm]and [Eb/Bb]died [Ab]on [Eb/G]earth [Cm]that [Ab]we might [Eb/Bb]live [Bbm]above.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Ab]Give of [Bbm]thine [Cm]own [Eb7/Bb]to [Ab]bear the message [Eb7]glorious;
[Db]give of thy [Ab]wealth to [Eb7]speed them on their [Ab]way;
[Ab]pour out thy soul for [Cm]them [Fm/C]in prayer [Cm]victorious;
[Bbm]O [Eb/Bb]Zion, [Ab]haste [Eb/G]to [Cm]bring [Ab]the brighter [Bbm]day.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Ab]He comes [Cm]again; [Ab]O Zion, ere [Eb7]thou meet [Fm]Him,
[Db]Make known to every [Eb7]heart His saving [Ab]grace;
[Ab]Let none whom He hath [Cm]ransomed [Fm/C]fail [Cm]to greet [Fm]Him,
[Bbm]Through [Eb/Bb]thy [Ab]neglect, [Cm]unfit [Ab]to [Eb/Bb]see [Bbm]His [Eb]face.
{end_of_verse}
